      "story_id": 1,
      "headline": "Pakistan hosts stalled US-Iran ceasefire talks as Munir and Shehbaz emerge as global mediators \u2014 then talks collapse",
      "summary": "Pakistan served as the venue and primary mediator for US-Iran ceasefire negotiations throughout the week, with Field Marshal Asim Munir and PM Shehbaz Sharif personally credited by Trump for securing a ceasefire extension. Iran FM Abbas Araghchi made two visits to Islamabad (April 25 and April 26\u201327), meeting Munir, Sharif, and FM Ishaq Dar; Trump dispatched envoys Witkoff and Kushner but then abruptly cancelled their trip on April 25; Iran left without direct talks and flew to Moscow, leaving the mediation effort in an uncertain state. Parallel sub-plots include: Iranian state media accusing Pakistan of a 'double game'; ISPR issuing an erroneous communiqu\u00e9 claiming US negotiators were already in Pakistan; Islamabad and Rawalpindi placed under near-lockdown for days; KP Assembly tabling a Nobel Peace Prize resolution for Sharif and Munir; extensive international profiling of Munir's rise; and Iran presenting an 'amended framework' proposal via Pakistan.",
